#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166440 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "d9715a0c-6808-5db8-b0b4-5bedc4f2e9e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-21155" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074064/assets/075eca4fcc837dce57c4bcfba01047af3d72f15b80cd3fabfc7e5b00be83813d.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$ \nFind the solution of the new system in terms of the parameter $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L\\,{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L\\,{-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L\\,{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L\\,{3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL\\,{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L\\,{{x}_{1}(t)}+L\\,{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL\\,{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=3L\\,{{x}_{1}(t)}-L\\,{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=-3{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-4=3{X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\!\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ -3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1){X}_{2}(s)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the first equation, we have\n\n$$\nX_2(s) = (s+3)X_1(s) - 4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1)\\,[(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4] & =4 \\\\ -3{X}_{1}(s)+(s+1)(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4(s+1) & =4 \\\\ [(s+1)(s+3)-3]{X}_{1}(s) & =4+4(s+1) \\\\ s(s+4){X}_{1}(s) & =4s+8 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $X_2(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{2}(s) & =(s+3){X}_{1}(s)-4 \\\\  & =(s+3)\\,(\\frac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)})-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s+3)(s+2)-4s(s+4)}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4({s}^{2}+5s+6)-4({s}^{2}+4s)}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{s}^{2}+20s+24-4{s}^{2}-16s}{s(s+4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(s+6)}{s(s+4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nX_1(s) =\\dfrac{4(s+2)}{s(s+4)}, \n\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{4(s+6)}{s(s+4)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166441 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/id #uuid "ec8e6fde-504e-581f-b465-6a9bc3927d77" :question/math-academy-id "e-21156" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074064/assets/243212bee1e50c7ca289142dcc8a9b5ac4f6d06fe3715661e99ec2601c82bf45.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ x_1(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{4}{s} + \\dfrac{1}{s-6}, \n\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{ x_2(t) \\right\\} = \\dfrac{20}{s} - \\dfrac{1}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem." :question/worked-solution "To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{20}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =20{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =20\\cdot 1-{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =20-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ 20-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166442 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd7b8fc8-26d3-5551-9a46-45725bd863a6" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/id #uuid "0b2a74d8-1ce2-5055-a843-1456b1878cf7" :question/math-academy-id "e-21157" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074064/assets/0be5433ffb8166a35fc9084c59116f77b223e25b85f939cb3c279f983939bc1f.png)\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXX}[/math]}}=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ \\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXX}[/math]}}=\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{XXXXXXXX}[/math]}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{9{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=9L{{x}_{1}(t)}+5L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-7=9{X}_{1}(s)+5{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81626a0-6613-5f5d-9dda-df853958c571" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35db50db-929a-58cf-aac5-10088f84f9c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9s-30}{s(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35db50db-929a-58cf-aac5-10088f84f9c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9s-30}{s(s-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380227} :answer-field/id #uuid "32855a04-54d2-565d-a5de-cad0c9bb1078" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "352d1492-cbac-52be-ab13-b4b1c7ef68ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-322291" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}-2L{{x}_{2}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)}+2L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-9={X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-6=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)=9 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-2){X}_{2}(s)=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =9 \\\\ 6(s-1)-[(s-1)(s-2)-2]{X}_{2}(s) & =9 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-3s){X}_{2}(s) & =9-6(s-1) \\\\ -s(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =-6s+15 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =6-(s-2){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =6-(s-2)\\cdot \\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6s(s-3)-3(s-2)(2s-5)}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3s-10)}{s(s-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3(3s-10)}{s(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3(2s-5)}{s(s-3)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd7b8fc8-26d3-5551-9a46-45725bd863a6" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e737318-3027-59e3-b434-d8298d2c8ce1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380230} {:answer/id #uuid "85fd245d-b2f8-55e6-8f38-de8bc36f0ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380231} {:answer/id #uuid "685b81e8-8766-5997-a492-69f9df088bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380232} {:answer/id #uuid "39e882c6-cd7d-57bc-8175-98de52c1f563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "685b81e8-8766-5997-a492-69f9df088bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380232} :answer-field/id #uuid "57a7f60b-a37a-58f4-8c0c-088fc38fdf80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "733aadbb-1a66-5848-b7c5-126082928bcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{2}(s)+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380235} {:answer/id #uuid "46dda2d8-5288-54d1-8943-0abc56d11108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{2}(s)+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380236} {:answer/id #uuid "563be134-1fe6-557c-a3b6-729731efb167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{2}(s)-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380237} {:answer/id #uuid "533f0506-14f1-5f4e-80ef-60be01774dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{2}(s)-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "533f0506-14f1-5f4e-80ef-60be01774dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{2}(s)-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380238} :answer-field/id #uuid "8db3f383-6d53-5c2b-9ab9-eaf96156f3ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04415e5-bcd2-5809-9c92-531cd9a0016e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380240} {:answer/id #uuid "6debdc4f-0cab-5492-9401-1afb51beb8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380241} {:answer/id #uuid "251accec-dba5-5ad4-aa3e-df1e1ea73962" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380242} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf3017a-6c97-572e-a30c-a9641e6c61e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6debdc4f-0cab-5492-9401-1afb51beb8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2}(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380241} :answer-field/id #uuid "91a7110e-0144-58cb-8d97-0fa86a7be0df" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2771b9b-89bc-5a83-829a-af6b6b2d190a" :question/math-academy-id "q-331891" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}=-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ {{field-2}}={{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-L{{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)}-4L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-7=-3{X}_{1}(s)-4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd7b8fc8-26d3-5551-9a46-45725bd863a6" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Laplace Transform to a System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "465855c4-4131-5b0e-bd93-b755dd12f444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380246} {:answer/id #uuid "d15d66a0-4dee-5dc5-bd98-79aa80e870c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380247} {:answer/id #uuid "61c1cd58-b623-5896-ad41-91a42b446a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380248} {:answer/id #uuid "d48d9f70-643c-5100-854a-5ae3feaa8081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{X}_{1}(s)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61c1cd58-b623-5896-ad41-91a42b446a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{1}(s)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380248} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac6d6e6b-3229-5521-a221-47d9c07d8f3e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380245} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6ed3644-f78c-5077-99a2-74940f5c406d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s{X}_{2}(s)+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380251} {:answer/id