\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}L{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)}=L{-3{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ L{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)}=L{2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}sL{{x}_{1}(t)}-{x}_{1}(0)=-3L{{x}_{1}(t)} \\\\ sL{{x}_{2}(t)}-{x}_{2}(0)=2L{{x}_{1}(t)}+L{{x}_{2}(t)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1=-3{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-5=2{X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-1=-3{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{1}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)-5=2(\\frac{1}{s+3})+{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{5s+17}{(s+3)(s-1)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca42235c-a157-5814-bd07-c8537787e429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca42235c-a157-5814-bd07-c8537787e429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380332} :answer-field/id #uuid "00f5b1ed-2a89-587a-b71a-5b036333f561" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51167137-cfbb-50f8-92ce-85d9d84e02f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51167137-cfbb-50f8-92ce-85d9d84e02f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380334} :answer-field/id #uuid "735edb87-96ef-564f-ba4f-f9dfea6c4b02" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcd588b4-8e9f-5afe-aacd-c8b798fd18aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcd588b4-8e9f-5afe-aacd-c8b798fd18aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380336} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba4125ad-060c-56fd-962e-491998af5815" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d56e172d-5930-569c-a2f8-b5750a9c8cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d56e172d-5930-569c-a2f8-b5750a9c8cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380338} :answer-field/id #uuid "37e39453-1eee-5f47-b122-19c3b99c0562" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380337}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e70dcec-ab6c-5150-a244-a01c0813cc93" :question/math-academy-id "q-332381" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{3}{s+1},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=-\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{4}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{2t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{s+1}} \\\\  & =3{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-1\\cdot t} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{-\\frac{1}{s+1}+\\frac{4}{s-2}} \\\\  & =-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+1}}+4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1\\cdot t}+4{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}+4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{-t}+4{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c566bed-0364-53d6-b686-0e2ff77e9995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380341} {:answer/id #uuid "6003bf10-8d7e-5648-9caf-da4fc474cac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6003bf10-8d7e-5648-9caf-da4fc474cac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 175921863803