(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-2}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{2t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+{e}^{2t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{2\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1-{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d9b08b5-a84b-54eb-b27b-9a952d8be990" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/