pe {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fee1caec-82d0-5ab4-b648-40120b354ab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-332409" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{2s}+\\frac{7}{2(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{3}{2s}-\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{4t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{2s}+\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s}-\\frac{7}{2(s-4)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-\\frac{7}{2}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 1-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4\\cdot t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{7}{2}{e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccbc4371-128b-5dc2-b9d9-d260c9bbbb5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccbc4371-128b-5dc2-b9d9-d260c9bbbb5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380360} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f3e2677-ba88-5ce0-b55f-f7d821ddad9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4930a06c-6584-554a-bcd3-bd1b564ab0bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4930a06c-6584-554a-bcd3-bd1b564ab0bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380362} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a302926-a276-5af4-875e-89378bdce800" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d4e28d5-1692-5776-b738-181b5fff15d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d4e28d5-1692-5776-b738-181b5fff15d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380364} :answer-field/id #uuid "9344212b-3309-57f8-8d3b-03802b04ec41" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380363} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3b1649a-8ec5-55c9-93a3-4ea247ecb1f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3b1649a-8ec5-55c9-93a3-4ea247ecb1f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380366} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7998742-37d8-5791-bdcb-ce7609ee29bc" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e21a0486-fb2c-5b77-8555-d2377681c5fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-332436" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{4}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{6t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s}+\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s}-\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1-{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =4-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4+{e}^{6t} \\\\ 4-{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f145cb40-80af-5381-9eb1-e4313dc74d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380369} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1d78c0-949c-528f-8beb-37bbf29e77cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a1d78c0-949c-528f-8beb-37bbf29e77cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380370} :answer-field/id #uuid "1703abfa-74ca-52fd-ad17-49aba47f88bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380368} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e50089e-3204-5873-aba4-2c07d6a8fe07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e50089e-3204-5873-aba4-2c07d6a8fe07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380372} :answer-field/id #uuid "f71c6f3b-0969-5fab-bf39-d74606b73d94" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d724a2dc-d391-5194-b17c-b322336aa9f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d724a2dc-d391-5194-b17c-b322336aa9f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380374} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff21a16d-b79f-5d1b-b6f6-fa722b5d7059" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45b8bd6a-4936-5407-b393-6664e229e87d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45b8bd6a-4936-5407-b393-6664e229e87d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380376} :answer-field/id #uuid "4886bca2-d6c5-5102-a0ae-3accb369ac9c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1d61f06-18e5-5c6e-a8d9-7b462e40a93d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332439" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{6t}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{1}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6}} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}+4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{{X}_{2}(s)} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}} \\\\  & =5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s}}-4{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-6}} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ 5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
